  (*TEMPORARY (`exception Option` hunt, 2026-08-14, user-approved).  ML_debugger
    instruments this session's own ML; ML_exception_debugger makes a failing
    command print the resulting call trace.  Both are needed: without the
    instrumentation Poly/ML has no stack to print, and then the report degrades
    to the bare raise line, which is what every earlier observation showed.
    Arming them here rather than on the command line means ANY ordinary build
    of this session catches the bug if it fires.
    (ML_exception_trace is useless on this Poly/ML -- its handler never fires.)
    TO REVERT: drop these two options, drop Option_Hunt_Probe from the theory
    list below, delete Phi_System/Option_Hunt_Probe.thy, and rebuild --
    instrumented heaps are slower.  See OPTION_EXCEPTION_IN_PROOF_REPLAY.md.*)
  options[document_build = build, ML_debugger = true, ML_exception_debugger = true]
